@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] rust-backend-preserves-client-boundary
The Rust rewrite MUST implement backend work without rewriting the web or Android UI.
Transport adapters MAY change to connect those clients. Its migration notes MUST name
remaining TypeScript runtime dependencies and unsupported features rather than claiming
parity that is not implemented (Tavi, 15 Oct 2026 21:21 UTC, Rust rewrite request).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] rust-verification-stays-lightweight
Verification of this rewrite MUST prioritize compilation and bounded compatibility
checks, not compute-intensive test suites or benchmarks (Tavi, 15 Oct 2026 21:21:47 UTC).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] rust-native-and-browser-methods-separated
The native HTTP API MUST keep storage and credential-proxy methods off its allowlist.
Browser-only methods MUST require the terminal-code session unless the operator explicitly
uses no-auth behind their authenticated proxy. Neither surface may return a GitHub token
(server-phone-method-allowlist and root github-token-stays-on-server contracts).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] rust-ai-capabilities-fail-closed
CLI jobs MUST have only the preselected PR context and dedicated job folder. If the
configured isolated runtime is unavailable the job MUST fail; it MUST NOT fall back to
an unrestricted host process (root agents-act-through-pr-tools contract).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] rust-source-snapshots-are-complete
Source fetching MUST reject truncated or capped file inventories. GitHub PR base/head
identities MUST be rechecked before publishing a fetched snapshot. Compare refs MUST
resolve before pagination. Git output and network bodies MUST be bounded, and Git
commands MUST time out without changing the checkout or index.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] rust-local-source-excludes-server-state
Working-tree source reads MUST exclude Git administration and the configured review
and analytics data directories, including symlink aliases. AI source tools MUST NOT
read the server's private state (agents-act-through-pr-tools; Rust review, 15 Oct 2026).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] rust-local-binary-identity-tracks-content
Untracked binary changes MUST contribute their complete byte content to file and
working-tree identities so changed files cannot retain stale review marks (Rust
correctness review, 15 Oct 2026; data-file-marks-follow-the-head).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] rust-inbox-refreshes-are-serialized
Concurrent inbox refreshes MUST share a serialized refresh and recheck fresh state
before fetching; an older overlapping result MUST NOT replace a newer snapshot
(Rust correctness review, 15 Oct 2026; existing SWR cache behavior).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] rust-backend-parity-is-observable
The Rust backend MUST preserve the existing clients' backend wire contracts for model
catalogs, streamed work, chat grouping, source tools, TypeSafe classification, compressed
sharing, persistent full-file caching and periodic preanalysis. It MUST NOT substitute
empty success responses for missing functionality (Tavi, 16 Oct 2026 05:01 UTC,
"Continue until you've fixed all the parity gaps").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] rust-container-tools-use-scoped-capabilities
A Docker job MAY call the native server through a random, per-run tool capability.
That capability MUST be valid only while its job is running, MUST be bound to the
selected immutable review context, and MUST NOT grant general RPC, storage or GitHub
credentials. Shared CLI login state MUST be copied as selected credential files into
an isolated job home; unrelated shared settings and skills MUST NOT reach the job. In the
hosted agent container, where jobs are plain processes, a job MUST run as a user that cannot
read the login homes (Tavi's 16 Oct parity request; agents-act-through-pr-tools; Tavi's 24 Oct
"Rewrite it as a Worker").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] rust-openui-inert-wire-parity
Brief parsing MUST preserve the locked OpenUI plain-tree behavior, including reactive
syntax as inert AST and the distinction between generated validation and recovered
saved trees. Input and expansion MUST be bounded; parsing MUST NOT execute actions,
tool calls, expressions or JavaScript (Tavi's 16 Oct parity request; core briefTree
and briefProblems contracts).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] rust-background-does-not-mark-viewed
Cache warming and preanalysis MUST NOT count as user views or overwrite a newly stored
head. Preanalysis MUST be opt-in and attempt each requested PR head at most once per
server lifetime, including failed attempts (Tavi's 16 Oct parity request; original
preanalysis-commits-observed-head and server-store-answers-first contracts).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] server-ai-work-outlives-the-page
Every Claude Code, Codex or Pi run a client starts is a server task. Reloading, closing a
tab or a phone sleeping MUST NOT stop or lose it: `abort()` cancels (Stop), `detach()`
only stops following. A running task doing the same work is joined, not started twice
(architecture, AI work outlives the page).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] server-follow-ups-run-on-the-server
What follows an analysis (`then`: tour, brief) is started by the server when the analysis
succeeds, so a phone that is asleep or closed still gets its tour; a tour that is already
current is not written again (architecture, AI work outlives the page).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] server-chat-needs-no-analysis
A chat with no saved analysis starts from the pull request itself with the same diff
tools, so Ask works on a pull request that was never analysed (rule 62; architecture).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] server-every-cli-through-start-agent
Every CLI process the server starts, jobs and the model catalog alike, MUST go through
`backend/src/agent_process.rs` and its Docker boundary. A CLI has only its job folder
read-write; its selected PR inputs and native helper are read-only, and repository
reads go through the PR tools. Stopping a run MUST kill its container. The native
runtime is Docker-only and MUST fail closed rather than run on the host (architecture,
Where the CLIs run; recording 14 Oct 19:19, 01:31; Tavi's 15 Oct 2026 Rust rewrite and
16 Oct 2026 parity requests, replacing the former host-or-Docker runtime). The one
exception is the hosted agent container, which is itself the sandbox: there `agent_runner`,
which refuses to start outside that image, runs the same jobs as plain processes with the
same job folder, inputs and PR tools, and stopping a run MUST kill its process (Tavi, 24 Oct
2026, "Rewrite it as a Worker"; packages/worker `hosted-ai-in-the-logins-own-container`).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] server-curated-skills-only
Review lenses come only from the curated skills. The server MUST NOT offer the skills of
the account it runs under (architecture, Where the CLIs run).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] server-pi-has-only-pr-tools
A Pi job gets exactly the PR tools the CLIs get over MCP and nothing more: no shell, files
or web. A LegacyPrivate Pi job's endpoint and key come only from its environment, and
without a base URL it fails with how to set it up (architecture, Pi). By Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 per-user provider decision and 22 Oct clarification that AI does not require
GitHub login, a separately authorized personal/local/default AI capability MAY supply
its own captured credential and model. That capability MUST retain its own owner,
allowance and revocation fence; it MUST NOT adopt legacy environment/CLI authority or
broaden the scoped PR tools.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] server-phone-method-allowlist
The phone may call only the methods allowed by `phone_allowed` in
`backend/src/transport.rs` and their native dispatch handlers. Storage methods and
anything that reads the GitHub token MUST stay off the list, and any other name answers
404 "That method is not available to the app."

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] server-typesafe-key-never-echoed
The TypeSafe key is read from the environment and sent only to TypeSafe. It MUST NOT be
echoed in an answer, an error, a notice, a log line, a work log, an AI prompt or a PR
payload; Jev's ratings reach an AI job through the PR payload, never the key
(architecture, Jev).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] server-jev-only-when-needed
Jev is asked only when something needs it: when a review of a whole diff starts, and
when a client asks `my-pulls-cached` with `classify: true`. Without a key, or once
TypeSafe refuses it, Jev is off for the run and nothing fails toward a client
(architecture, Jev).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] server-my-pulls-never-waits-for-jev
`my-pulls` MUST NOT wait for Jev, and an answer for an older head or title MUST NOT
replace a newer one (architecture, Jev).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] server-store-answers-first
Opening a pull request MUST NOT wait on every page of its files. The server keeps the
open pull requests stored and answers from the store when GitHub's head has not moved; a
store write MUST NOT replace a head stored after it read, and warming MUST NOT count as a
view (architecture, The phone reads the server's store; H14).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] server-repositories-warm-ahead
The server keeps the first page of each repository the Inbox shows most, so a
repository's page opens at once (H14).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] server-refreshes-by-itself
The server notices new commits on its own, so an open pull request takes them without a
Refresh (rule 52; H11).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] server-stacks-from-branches
A pull request's stack comes from GitHub's own stacks where the host has them, otherwise
from branches in one repository (A sits on B when A's base is B's head); a fork's branch
never counts and the default branch is always the bottom (DESIGN.md decision log,
0.20.0).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] server-ai-writes-links
The analysis, tour, Ask and review instructions tell the model to write every place it
names as a repository-relative link, and a check makes sure they do ("super, super,
super important", rule 96; F43).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] server-posted-links-point-at-the-head
Text posted to GitHub (comments, reviews, shared results) has its links read from the
repository root and rewritten to `github.com/{owner}/{repo}/blob/{headSha}/...` first,
dot-folders kept, so no link 404s (rules 96 and 124; J36; architecture, Sharing).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] server-catalog-text-models-only
The model catalog lists each model once and only models that write text: image and other
generation models (GPT Image, Grok Imagine Image) are left out, since Pulls never makes
images (recording 15 Oct 13:54, 00:22 to 00:44; K2, K4).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] server-follow-ups-by-a-small-model
The follow-up questions under an Ask answer are written each turn by a small, fast model,
not the one answering (rule 99; F70).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] server-serves-the-android-build
The server MUST serve `/download` as an HTML page listing only Android artifacts
actually present with valid published metadata. The latest manifest and APK MUST use
`/download/latest.json` and `/download/pully.apk`, with `Cache-Control: no-store`;
unpublished artifacts MUST answer 404. `/android/pulls.apk` MUST answer 404, without a
redirect or SPA fallback. The old latest-manifest and history metadata/assets MAY
remain read-only aliases for installed clients, but their manifest MUST name the
new binary URL and MUST NOT name the HTML page as an installer. Historical apps MUST
be described honestly as side-by-side versions opened through Pully. Source: Tavi's
repeated 22 Oct 2026 request for the HTML download page, available real versions and
removal of the old direct APK route.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] server-new-chat-keeps-the-old-one
The phone's "new chat" (`chat-clear`) MUST set the current chat aside in the diff's chat
history, not throw it away, and a new analysis does the same with the chat after the old
one. `chat-history` lists the earlier chats most recent first as `{ chats: [{ id, title,
at, turns }] }`, and `chat-restore` puts one back as the current chat, setting the current
one aside first when it asked anything; an unknown id fails with a plain error. None of
them MAY change the analysis transcript before `chatStartIndex`. A diff keeps at most 30
earlier chats ("make this button a chat history button ... a list of the chats for this PR
that you've already gone into", recording 15 Oct 2026 15:37, L36).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] server-tour-previews-reach-the-phone
A tour's `tour-plan` and `tour-stop:<index>` work-log entries reach the phone through the
task snapshots with their `text` whole: nothing between native tour generation and
`ai-task-wait` MAY cut or drop it, since the phone builds its previews of the tour from
that JSON (recording 15 Oct 2026 15:37, L26).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] server-pi-effort-in-the-id
A Pi model whose id names a reasoning effort (`gemini-3.8-flash-high`, `gpt-5.5(high)`,
shown as "(High)") MUST offer that effort alone, as its default, and a run on it MUST NOT
send a reasoning effort beside the id ("just assume that that's the reasoning effort, and
when I select them, the only reasoning effort they have is that one", recording 15 Oct
2026 15:37, L24).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] server-posts-exact-critique
Posting AI findings MUST retrieve the displayed variant and match its immutable
content revision and expected head. Every selected ID MUST resolve before contacting
GitHub; another result MUST NOT silently replace the selected review (repository
review 15 Oct 2026, finding 8).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] server-chat-state-is-complete
The native saved chat response MUST return complete message text without silent
truncation, including after clearing and restoring a conversation (repository review
15 Oct 2026, finding 21; ask-streams-and-cites).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] web-github-operations-stay-server-side
The local web client MUST receive GitHub operation results, never the server's raw GitHub
credential. Its GitHub transport MUST restrict requests to the GitHub API origin and MUST
NOT follow redirects with server credentials (Tavi, 15 October 2026, fix the full-review
findings, issue 5; github-token-stays-on-server).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] web-cache-writes-preserve-server-state
Local web diff mutations MUST execute through the shared server diff repository; raw
browser writes MUST NOT replace its split metadata or body documents. Other browser
cache writes MUST reject a changed last-observed value (Tavi, 15 October 2026, fix the
full-review findings, issue 6; server-store-answers-first).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] jobs-codex-pr-tools-only
Every Codex job MUST disable shell_tool, unified_exec and view_image; repository reads
go through the PR MCP tools (agents-act-through-pr-tools; review finding 2, 15 Oct 2026).
The native runtime permits only isolated Docker jobs, with no host fallback (Tavi's
15 Oct 2026 Rust rewrite and 16 Oct 2026 parity requests).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] jobs-release-acquired-slots
A job that acquired a concurrency slot MUST release it and settle even if temporary
directory creation fails. Its execution timeout MUST exclude queue time
(review findings 3 and 18, 15 Oct 2026).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] task-conversations-validate-storage
Persisted question threads and inbox turns MUST be runtime-validated before use;
malformed nested entries MUST NOT prevent valid conversation history from loading
(engine-shapes-are-schemas; review finding 19, 15 Oct 2026).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] task-chat-history-serializes-writers
Clearing or restoring a chat MUST cancel active replies and wait for their session
writes before selecting the conversation; later chats MUST read the selected session
(recording 15 Oct 2026 15:37, L36; review finding 28).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] native-rpc-honors-declared-schemas
Native calls MUST validate every declared argument before invoking its handler and
pass the validator's transformed value. Declared return schemas MUST also be checked
before sending a result (repository review 15 Oct 2026, finding 20).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] preanalysis-commits-observed-head
Preanalysis MUST save its diff, analysis and transcript only when the stored head has
not changed since the run began. Its writes MUST NOT count as views
(server-store-answers-first; review finding 4, 15 Oct 2026).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] server-session-shares-state
RPCs, native requests, tasks and preanalysis for one principal and credential binding
MUST share its AppState storage and cache coordinator. Guest and personal account
contexts MUST NOT share the legacy private server's state or another account's state.
Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 personal-account/public-browsing decision replaces the former global
scope; the existing LegacyPrivate context retains its shared instance
(server-ai-work-outlives-the-page; review finding 6, 15 Oct 2026).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] tenant-ai-never-inherits-operator-login
Nonlegacy contexts MUST NOT start AI work, query operator model catalogs or seed the
operator's environment account until an explicit personal provider authority and budget
have been installed for that context. Public ingress MUST remain unavailable until its
own allowlist, session validation and tenant isolation are implemented and reviewed.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 request for each user's own Claude/ChatGPT/Pi connection.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] stored-opening-keeps-newer-heads
A fetch MUST NOT replace a head stored since this opening observed the cache, including
fresh and cold opens; it MUST return the winning stored diff instead
(server-store-answers-first; review finding 22, 15 Oct 2026).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] engine-worktree-reads-stay-in-repository
Working-tree reads MUST resolve the repository and target before checking containment,
reject escaping file or directory symlinks, and check the opened descriptor where the OS
supports it (requested review fixes, 15 Oct 2026, finding #9).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] server-reaches-the-machine-through-its-host
The phone API, the server session, the review routes and the PR store reach storage, the
checkout and served files only through their the native host boundary, so the same code runs on a
computer and on a hosted server (message 16 Oct 08:39, "where we want to host the server
... to make sure that it's actually faster"; `plans/12-hosted-server.md`). The native host MUST NOT require a Node runtime. A host without a checkout answers `NO_CHECKOUT` on every local
route and MUST NOT fall back to the server's working directory.


@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] server-past-versions-answer-empty
`GET /download/past/index.json`, which the phone reads, and its `/android/past/index.json`
alias answer `{ "versions": [] }` while no past version is built,
never a 404, so the phone says none are built yet rather than that the server did not
answer. `publish-apk.sh` writes the index at once and builds the past versions in the
background, newest first, adding each to the index as it is built (recording 16 Oct 2026
09:50, 01:09 to 01:14; M3).


@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] server-github-stats-counts-only
`github-stats` answers the signed-in user's last year on GitHub as counts only (totals,
contributions per day, streaks, followers and repositories), reused for a few minutes and
fetched with the server's own GitHub token; no repository name, title or text is in it
(recording 16 Oct 2026 09:50, 02:06 to 02:16; M5).


@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] server-account-from-the-environment
The password test account is `PULLY_ACCOUNT_EMAIL` and `PULLY_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD`, seeded
on first use and updated when they change; there is no password registration endpoint.
Google sign-in follows `google-sign-in-same-account`; `account-status` answers
`hasAccount: true` when either password seeding or the Google client ID is configured.
After five wrong passwords in fifteen minutes password sign-in waits, even for the right one (Tavi, 16 Oct 12:40: "you don't need to add
any register functionality ... you can just seed the database").


@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] server-posted-diffs-kept-forever
A posted diff is stored as the agent sent it, the patch and its fields, and everything
else is worked out again from them; the cache budget MUST NOT evict it and only a DELETE
removes it, with everything kept under its key (Tavi, 16 Oct 12:40: "Link is actually
forever", "store what the agent gave us as opposed to the final result").


@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] server-posted-links-from-the-environment
The link a post answers is `PULLY_PUBLIC_URL` (such as `https://prs.octaviantocan.com`)
followed by `/-/<id>`, or the request's own origin when it is unset (Tavi, 16 Oct 12:40:
"the domain should probably just be like an environment variable").


@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] server-posted-refuses-secrets
A post whose added lines look like a key or token, or that adds a `.env` file, is refused
with 422 naming the file, line and kind, never the secret itself, unless the agent says
`allowSecrets` (plan "Posted diffs", Safety).


@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] server-agent-results-checked
An agent MAY send its own groups, tour, brief and review with a post (Tavi, 16 Oct 12:40:
"the agent can actually add its own grouping and tour"). Each is checked against its
schema and against the diff: a path the diff does not have is dropped with a warning in
the answer, and a part that does not fit is left out with a warning, so the post itself
still goes through.


@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] server-settings-newer-wins
The account's synced settings are merged one setting at a time: a value replaces the
kept one only when its time is newer, so two phones never undo each other's other
choices, and merges of one account run one at a time. At most 200 settings are kept, each
at most 8 KB and 64 KB in all (Tavi, 16 Oct 12:47).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] rust-browser-cache-transport-budget
Authenticated browser cache RPCs MUST accept serialized supported source diffs above
4 MiB while retaining finite wire and decoded-graph bounds; small authentication and
analytics endpoints MUST keep their separate limits (R12 parity fix, 16 Oct 2026).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] rust-websocket-preauth-buffer-bound
WebSocket frame and unfinished-message buffering MUST use the small authentication
budget until a verified upgrade-time credential grants the browser cache budget.
Code exchange MUST remain usable by reconnecting with the issued token before large
browser RPCs (R14 security finding 3, 16 Oct 2026; rust-browser-cache-transport-budget).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] rust-agent-post-attempts-are-limited
Invalid POST and PUT submissions MUST consume the authenticated agent key's hourly
allowance before body or patch validation. An exhausted key MUST receive 429 with a
positive Retry-After; another key and requests after the hourly window retain their
allowance (R14 parity finding 6, 16 Oct 2026; original agent-API limit fixture).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] rust-final-login-helper-is-cleaned
Job cleanup MUST stop model and bootstrap containers before final credential
persistence, then retry named-container removal after that final helper, including
when Docker finishes creating after its client times out. Shutdown MUST await this
cleanup before releasing the job folder (R14 reliability finding 7, 16 Oct 2026).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] rust-browser-origin-matches-listener
Browser origin checks and startup URLs MUST use the actual bound port, including when
port zero selects one, bracket IPv6 literals, and omit HTTP's default port like browser
Origin headers (Tavi, 16 Oct 19:27 UTC, final operational setup/parity request).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] rust-native-failures-reach-analytics
Failed responses from account and general native RPC handlers MUST record one error.server event
through the existing analytics privacy/opt-out boundary, without replacing dispatched
RPC timing events or changing response bodies (Tavi, 16 Oct 19:27 UTC, operational
parity request; main native-api.ts noteFailure behavior).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] server-feedback-kept-for-agents
Feedback sent from the phone (`feedback-send`, which needs the account's session) is kept
under that account with the server's own time, the app's version and versionCode, the
screen and pull request it was sent from, the device and its Android or iOS version, the theme and
the language, and nothing the client names for itself such as the account or a status. It
is never evicted. The account's keys read it newest first at `GET /api/v1/feedback`
(`?status=open|done`) and `GET /api/v1/feedback/<id>`, and `PATCH` marks it `done` with an
optional note on what was done, or `open` again; no other account sees it, and its words
MUST NOT reach usage analytics ("a button somewhere for me to leave feedback from the app
itself ... It obviously needs to be stored with timestamps, app version, etc": Tavi, 20 Oct
2026 06:10; iOS metadata added by Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 same-app iOS request).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] rust-ios-analytics-keeps-the-existing-cleaner
The first-party analytics endpoint MUST accept the native ios app label through the
same event, content redaction, size, batching and retention policy as Android/web.
Unknown app labels MUST remain rejected; enabling iOS MUST NOT bypass the cleaner or
add a telemetry service. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 full shared iOS app request and
root analytics-stays-on-our-server and analytics-what-not-how-much.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] ai-runs-on-the-callers-own-sign-in
AI runs and model lists for a signed-in Pully account MUST use only that account's own
Claude Code and Codex sign-in, kept in its own login volume; they MUST NOT use another
account's or the server's sign-in, and a session that no longer names an account MUST be
refused rather than fall back. A running run MUST NOT be joined by another login's
identical request. Requests without a Pully account and the server's own background work
use the server's sign-in from setup.sh. Claude Code and Codex MUST NOT be given an API
key (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, OPENAI_API_KEY) on any path. Source:
Tavi, 23 Oct 2026 13:39: "Claude Code and Codex SUBSCRIPTION login. Not any other kind
of thing. I don't even care to implement API Key for those. We need to be able to use
people's subscription usage."

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] ai-sign-in-is-the-clis-own
A sign-in MUST run the unmodified CLI's own login (`claude auth login --claudeai`,
`codex login --device-auth`) in a container holding only that login's volume (hosted:
that login's own agent container), with no job inputs, PR tools or prompt. The server MUST
NOT read the resulting tokens; it passes the person's pasted code only to that CLI's stdin.
It MUST NOT store them either, except that the hosted server keeps each login's sign-in
files as text in that login's own `AgentHome` Durable Object while its container sleeps
(Tavi, 24 Oct 2026 19:27, "store them as text in there or something and convert back to
whatever file or token the CLIs need"). Only a signed-in Pully
account MAY start, finish or sign out a sign-in. The phone MUST be given only links on
the providers' own sign-in hosts, and status MUST count only subscription sign-ins
(claude.ai, ChatGPT), never a Console or API key login. Source: Tavi, 23 Oct 2026 13:39,
and Anthropic's Claude Code legal and compliance page checked that day ("sign-in to a
Claude account must complete through Anthropic's own flow"; hosting the unmodified
binary for users who sign in with their own subscription is allowed).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] server-builds-for-workers
The library MUST build for `wasm32-unknown-unknown` as well as natively, so the hosted server is
this code running in a Worker (`packages/worker`). Code outside the native-only modules MUST use
`rt` for tasks, timers, environment, files and programs, `net` for outbound HTTP and
`store::Records` for storage, never tokio's runtime, `std::env` or reqwest's `send` directly. In
the Worker, files and programs MUST fail closed and outbound HTTP MUST NOT follow redirects (Tavi,
24 Oct 2026, "Rewrite it as a Worker"; plan 12, Update 24 Oct).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security;architecture] personal-workspace-is-the-full-native-service-for-its-own-account
The fixed POST /workspace/api/rpc route MUST require a previously confirmed canonical
personal-vault session with the explicit privateRepositories grant. It MUST reuse the
